# Gate step 1325-ygq5 — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. A test added in either organ can be referenced by nothing, and
# nothing said so at push time — so a fixture that CANNOT FAIL A GATE read
# identically to one that guards something.
#
# THE RULE IS ONE SENTENCE AND IT IS ORGAN-INDEPENDENT: A TEST IS NOT DONE UNTIL
# SOMETHING THAT RUNS ON ITS OWN CAN FAIL BECAUSE OF IT.
#
# TWO SPECIMENS, SAME HOST, SAME DAY (2026-09-20/21, pirria). A litmus yaml
# written into openspec/litmus-tests/ and never added to the bindings: a
# ci-release suite ran to completion reporting 37 PASS / 3 FAIL with that test
# in NEITHER number, and it was reported to the coordinator as verified. Then,
# hours later, a shell test committed with no step, no build.sh line and no
# binding — written to REPLACE an arm that counted MENTIONS of a flag instead of
# running the binary. It replaced a test that could not fail for the reason it
# named with one that could not fail at all.
#
# WHY THE LESSON DID NOT FIRE THE SECOND TIME. The first was filed against the
# ORGAN — a litmus yaml needs a bindings entry — rather than against the SHAPE,
# so nothing in the author's head matched when the artifact was a shell script.
# This step is filed against the shape, and the guard treats both organs as one
# question with two needles.
#
# WHY THE AUTHOR IS THE ONE PERSON WHO CANNOT SEE IT, and why a checklist is the
# weak form. Both organs' artifacts run green when invoked by hand, which is how
# an author checks; the file states its own spec and phase, or prints its own
# ok: line, so everything the author looks at says the test is real. Only the
# thing that never ran knows, and it reports the absence as a SMALLER TOTAL
# rather than as an error. A checklist at authoring time is read by the same
# person who has just finished the file and believes it is done.
#
# WHAT THIS STEP RUNS is the guard's FIXTURE, not the guard: the arms that
# matter are the refusals, and a guard for "this test cannot fail a gate" that
# has only ever been observed passing is this packet's own defect one level up.
# Mutation-proven — blanking the counter reds 3 arms, dropping the grandfather
# affordance reds 1, a silent green on a missing manifest reds 1.
#
# MIGRATION PHASE. The guard WARNS rather than refuses and carries the standing
# count (40 unreferenced shell tests on trunk, 2026-09-21) so the flip is a
# decision made AGAINST A NUMBER rather than on a date. Diff-scoped either way:
# it fires on what a push ADDS, never on the standing corpus, because a guard
# that refuses all forty turns one host's mistake into every host's red — the
# construction check-added-fragments-parse.sh uses for the same reason
# (698-7n6q). This step's fixture is hermetic and does not depend on the count.
#
# THE REFERENCE SURFACE IS DECLARED, not inline:
# scripts/test-reference-surfaces.manifest is the one definition both the guard
# and a reader use, and the verdict line carries its size. The packet's own
# unscoreable named this as the choice to make — 'referenced by' was four places
# and declared in none, so a fifth caller added tomorrow would have made
# referenced tests look unreferenced and started naming innocent files.
#
# THE NEGATIVE CONTROL IS THE POINT OF THE GRANDFATHER LIST. A deliberately
# unreferenced artifact must stay possible, or the guard converts a real
# practice into a lie. scripts/unreferenced-grandfathered.txt is the shell
# organ's sibling of the litmus organ's unbound-grandfathered.txt (660-ryhn),
# and it starts EMPTY: diff-scoping already covers the standing corpus, so a
# name written there is a live declaration someone should read and question.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose: a binding assembled from a variable
# is invisible to every name-based scan, including the bound-or-retired guard
# (1063-nraf). Keep it a plain string.
STEP_DESC="Checking an added test is referenced by something that runs on its own (1325-ygq5)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-added-test-is-referenced.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the guard that names an unreferenced added test no longer refuses (1325-ygq5) — read which arm failed above; the ENFORCE=1, missing-manifest and grandfather arms are the load-bearing ones, and a failure in the clean-pass arm alone is the least of them"
STEP_OK="An added test that nothing can fail because of is named at push time"
